* Task 7 fixture: PROCESS SQL with opaque body DDM edge + host-var scan
* Demonstrates FR-19/FR-21 / OQ-3 requirements:
*   - PROCESS SQL <DDM> emits one EdgeReads for the DDM operand (neutral read-style per OQ-3)
*   - Opaque body contains: bare table name (NOT a DDM edge — modeled gap),
*     plain colon host var (#PERS-ID), qualifier form (:U:#NAME and :G:#X),
*     and SQL keyword (SELECT) — none of these except host vars become edges
*   - Host vars from the opaque body are extracted with colon+qualifier stripped
*   - In-body SQL keywords and table names are NOT host-var refs
* Expected:
*   - extractSQLAccess emits exactly ONE EdgeReads for DDM "EMPLOYEE-DATA" (the ddm-name operand)
*   - extractHostVarRefs emits HostVarRefs for :#PERS-ID, :U:#NAME, :G:#X (qualifier-stripped)
*   - NO EdgeReads for in-body table name SALARY_TABLE (the load-bearing modeled gap)
*   - NO HostVarRef for SELECT keyword or SALARY_TABLE name

DEFINE DATA LOCAL
  1 #PERS-ID (N9)
  1 #NAME (A30)
  1 #X (N5)
END-DEFINE

PROCESS SQL EMPLOYEE-DATA
  << SELECT EMP_ID, EMP_NAME FROM SALARY_TABLE
     WHERE PERS_ID = :#PERS-ID
       AND NAME = :U:#NAME
       AND EXTRA = :G:#X >>

END
